  "tips": [
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l01-b-t01",
      "before": "kpk1-l01-b-e01",
      "title": {
        "en": "The Polish alphabet"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "The *alfabet* has 32 letters. Nine of them carry a mark: *ą ć ę ł ń ó ś ź ż*. There is no *q*, *v* or *x* in Polish words. Two letters can make one sound: *sz*, *cz*, *rz*, *ch*, *dz*, *dź*, *dż*."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "kpk1-l01-b-t02",
      "before": "kpk1-l01-b-e09",
      "title": {
        "en": "Spelling a word"
      },
      "body": {
        "en": "Asked *proszę przeliterować*, say each letter of the word: *dom* is d, o, m. Letters with a mark are said with their mark: *ł* is not *l*, and *ó* sounds the same as *u*. *Rz* and *ż* sound the same too, so a word is often spelled to be sure."
      }
    }
  ],
